# NOTICE

Third party code and models used by this repository. Every method traces back to
a publication, see `SETTINGS.md` for the citation and the settings.

## Withheld method

**StyloSpeaker** (Aggazzotti and Smith, https://github.com/caggazzotti/styloSpeaker)
is evaluated in the paper but is not part of this repository. The upstream
implementation carries no license, and our request to its authors for permission
has gone unanswered. The German adaptation kept several of its feature functions
close to verbatim, so redistributing it would require that permission. Until it
is granted, the method is left out of the pipeline and its results are not
published with this repository.

## Vendored source

**methods/dv/external/diff-vectors** is a partial copy of
https://github.com/AlexMoreo/diff-vectors (Corbara, Moreo and Sebastiani).
Six of the 28 Python files are included, byte for byte unchanged:
`feature_extraction/author_vectorizer.py`, `model/pair_classification.py`,
`model/pair_generator.py`, `utils/calibration.py`, `utils/common.py`,
`utils/lightweight_random_indexing.py`. The remaining files are dataset
fetchers, plotting and LaTeX table generators that this repository does not
import, and they were removed. Nothing was modified. The German adaptation
subclasses the upstream FeatureExtractor rather than editing it.

**diff-vectors is licensed GPL-2.0.** Distributing it here makes this a combined
work under section 2 of that license.

## Derived source

**methods/lambdag/custom_lambdag.py** is a copy of `lambdag.lambdag.LambdaGMethod`
from LambdaG 0.1.1 (MIT), extended by an optional process pool and by
`fit_predict`. The Kneser-Ney language model is imported from the package
unchanged. https://pypi.org/project/LambdaG/#files

**methods/coav**, **methods/mlsr**, **methods/mstyledistance** and
**methods/meta** derive from an internal implementation that is not public.

**methods/fevec** keeps the feature functions of the original implementation as
close to verbatim as the German adaptation allows. License: Apache-2. Original source: https://github.com/janithnw/pan2021_authorship_verification.

**methods/rsp** and **methods/css** are reimplementations from their papers, not
forks. RSP shares no function with https://github.com/peterzeng/rsp, which
carries no license. CSS has no public implementation.

